\description{
Abstract R6 class defining the interface shared by all MuData backends
(\link{InMemoryMuData}, \link{HDF5MuData}, \link{ZarrMuData}). It mirrors
\code{anndataR::AbstractAnnData}: slots are active bindings, operations are
methods, and standard R generics (\code{dim()}, \code{[[}, \code{print()}, ...) are
provided as S3 methods.

Global observation and variable names are stored separately from the
\code{obs}/\code{var} data frames, as in anndataR and Python.
}
\section{Slots (active bindings)}{

\itemize{
\item \code{mod}: a \link{ModalityMapping} of the modalities, each a genuine anndataR
AnnData object of the matching backend
\item \code{obs}, \code{var}: global annotation data frames
\item \code{obsm}, \code{varm}, \code{obsp}, \code{varp}, \code{uns}: aligned, pairwise and unstructured
global annotation
\item \code{obsmap}, \code{varmap}: named lists of integer maps (0 = absent, otherwise a
one-based position in the modality)
\item \code{obs_names}, \code{var_names}: global names
\item \code{axis}: \code{0} (shared observations), \code{1} (shared variables) or \code{-1} (both)
\item \code{filename}, \code{isbacked}, \code{is_view}: read-only
}
}

